"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2329e0063669ee2995389b0364191048937954389d5466f0819135db28c24738","event_uuid":"7040ed43-c030-490c-ab38-99274c10853f","position":{"commit_sha":"5551a59bd47822353ebc3600b4fe0abd4e172609","position":"1784776789315872001-7040ed43-c030-490c-ab38-99274c10853f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"71648ddb8c7f02bc0c6073ceb32327bc193694193ee61d88b4e79a7684efa881","event_uuid":"864043f1-481d-47c7-8499-55971bbd658d","position":{"commit_sha":"46c09e5f7f3048acd27e78c686e6c1b30cb5d85e","position":"1784776791538936001-864043f1-481d-47c7-8499-55971bbd658d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PASS advisory dispositions: f92d6649bb0e0ba08, f99d50689570cabed, f793e912beab1eea5, and fe0ed66d14c604180 are accepted as one implementation constraint. The audit integration belongs in build_context/page assembly after audit_trail has produced best-effort stored data; it passes the available attestation, reduced ticket state, and repo root to compute_validity. Missing attestation, unexpected output, timeout, or exception must be caught at that boundary, logged, and rendered as clearly labeled derived-health unavailable without changing audit_trail never-raise behavior. Close remains governed by the existing validity gate and surfaces a human-readable failure; display failures never silently change allow/deny semantics. Also accept f102b0bc723751f16: advanced docs include pin-enforcement toggles and close-versus-claim freshness. Accept f70baef9b8bd44bcc for execution: include the actual close-error renderer command path after tracing its existing owner. Schema changes are additive, preserving existing fields and rollback compatibility.","timestamp":1784575896144559001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit patchset 1 CI exposed one stale golden-path assertion in scripts/probe-rebar.sh: detailed show now intentionally adds plan_review_health while lean list remains unchanged. Updated only the expected detailed-only key delta; local isolated probe is 140 passed, 0 failed. Amended same Change-Id for patchset 2.","timestamp":1784775390928734001}],"created_at":1784517379286643001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"64d93ccc-84bf-4aa6-9508-c3c64d962f37","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"75de-02b0-d454-410b"},{"link_uuid":"18f9a363-2b18-4fe5-ae42-b70a778cd677","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"5967-4476-7f9f-442d"},{"link_uuid":"c702b4e6-cd9e-4fbe-9426-61a5b734c20c","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2bbd-87f6-8765-4b00"}],"description":"# Surface derived plan-review relationship health\n\n## Goal\nMake pin drift, enforcement posture, and review-phase compatibility understandable wherever operators inspect detailed review evidence, without adding noise to ordinary ticket lists or persisting warning events.\n\n## Implementation\n- Consume the validity story's DerivedPlanReviewHealth contract in detailed CLI show, MCP ticket detail, audit output, close errors, and the web ticket-review UI. Renderers must not define independent status strings.\n- Display each canonical related ticket, normalized role, pinned/current fingerprint status, missing-target state, enforcement effect, signed review phase, required phase, and effective execution floor as applicable.\n- When pin enforcement is disabled, label observed drift advisory and keep the overall validity presentation true. Clearly distinguish legacy-unpinned from current-no-relationships.\n- Keep ordinary list output and stored ticket events unchanged.\n- Update stable schemas/output models and their compatibility tests.\n- Document plan-material-pin, phase metadata, rollout behavior, deletion repair, and validity profiles in advanced plan-review/attestation documentation only; do not add it to basic user docs.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Audit rendering calls compute_validity and displays enabled pin invalidity.\n- [ ] Every detailed renderer consumes DerivedPlanReviewHealth without recreating status strings.\n- [ ] CLI show, MCP detail, audit text/JSON, close errors, and web review UI render the same derived health semantics with canonical IDs and actionable drift reasons.\n- [ ] Enforcement-off drift is visibly advisory, legacy-unpinned is distinguishable, and ordinary list output plus persisted events remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Output schemas, rendering tests, and advanced documentation cover pins, phases, toggles, deleted targets, and close-versus-claim freshness.\n\n## Verification\n- Run focused audit, rendering, MCP schema, and CLI golden tests.\n- Exercise the web audit page with current, drifted, disabled, legacy, and missing-target fixtures.\n- Run make check and the non-integration test suite.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/audit/read.py","reason":"Expose shared derived plan-review health in audit data."},{"path":"src/rebar/audit/page.py","reason":"Prepare health for web rendering."},{"path":"src/rebar/audit/templates/_gate_section.html","reason":"Render pin and phase health in the web review UI."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_audit_commands.py","reason":"Render detailed CLI audit health."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"Extend the MCP ticket-detail schema."},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"Document the advanced attestation and validity contract."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","2bbd-87f6-8765-4b00"],["depends_on","5967-4476-7f9f-442d"],["depends_on","75de-02b0-d454-410b"],["parent","jira-reb-1160"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"jira-reb-1160","parent_status_uuid":"7040ed43-c030-490c-ab38-99274c10853f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["plan-review","jira-reb-1160"],"ticket_id":"cb6b-24b4-1056-4ee6","ticket_type":"story","title":"Expose plan-material-pin health in detailed review surfaces and advanced docs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["97fcde10-f5f4-4172-bd73-4744eec2ac09","1a132a24-fc40-4f99-838e-f0fc3e7fea97","64d93ccc-84bf-4aa6-9508-c3c64d962f37","18f9a363-2b18-4fe5-ae42-b70a778cd677","c702b4e6-cd9e-4fbe-9426-61a5b734c20c","85e739b5-ae8b-4553-aa7d-4fd8fe9f984c","c1c85188-f994-45b9-b50e-9044c108ddc4","6ef62ff3-91ff-4bfc-b5c8-60710e4b382a","6c8285c9-4e04-4c87-bfa3-f44738eecec9","e3d3247e-782b-48ab-9555-a3be0c259e96","ef72164b-b46e-4f27-996d-994a31bd86bc","9f11e006-9696-4e08-8e55-69e15e7eb0e4","9441bd89-d74e-4baf-a772-bafa668cb5a2","7040ed43-c030-490c-ab38-99274c10853f","864043f1-481d-47c7-8499-55971bbd658d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659665213077001,"uuid":"cf242018-b34b-4564-8c61-87276c743113"}